# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the meetrao project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
- Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to integrate Vercel Web Analytics
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body tag in the root layout

### 3. Framework-Specific Implementation
- Used Next.js App Router specific implementation as documented in the official Vercel docs
- Followed the recommended pattern for Next.js 13+ with App Router
- Placed the Analytics component in the root layout to track all pages

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`) following the official Vercel documentation guidelines. The component is placed after the ToastProvider but before the closing body tag, ensuring it can track page views across the entire application.

The implementation follows Next.js App Router best practices and preserves all existing code structure, fonts, metadata, and the ToastProvider configuration.

## Verification

All verification steps completed successfully:
✓ Build completed without errors (`npm run build`)
✓ Linter passed without issues (`npm run lint`)
✓ All tests passed (17/17 tests in vitest)
✓ TypeScript compilation successful
✓ No regressions introduced

## Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under Analytics
3. After deployment, verify tracking by checking for a Fetch/XHR request to `/<unique-path>/view` in the browser's Network tab

The analytics will automatically start collecting data once deployed to Vercel with Analytics enabled in the dashboard.
